## What announcements are for

Announcements are one-way notices to parents — "sports day moved to Friday" — as opposed to
[reports](/docs/kindercare-staff-reports), which are about one child. They live on the **Notices**
tab of the staff app and behind the bell icon in the parent app.

## Posting one

**Notices → New announcement**, then:

1. **Title** and **Message** — both required.
2. **Send to** — who should receive it:
   - **All classes** — every parent in the school. Class teachers don't see this option; it is
     reserved for roles with school-wide reach.
   - **Classes** — pick one or more classes. A class teacher can only choose their own class, which
     is preselected.
   - **Students** — pick individual children from the selected classes, and **only those children's
     parents** are told.
3. **Also send an SMS** — off by default. Parents **always** get a push notification; the SMS option
   texts them as well, and costs money for each recipient, so leave it off unless the notice is
   urgent.

**Post Announcement** asks you to confirm first, naming the audience (for example "the parents of 2
classes"). Parents are sent a push notification when it is posted.

## Finding and removing announcements

The Notices tab lists what you've posted and filters by **All**, **School-wide**, **Classes** and
**Students**. Pull down to refresh; the list loads more as you scroll. The trash icon deletes an
announcement after a confirmation — a deleted notice is removed, so only delete one you posted by mistake.

## What parents see

Parents see a red badge on the bell for notices they haven't opened, and the full list under
**Announcements**. Unread ones are bold. See [The KinderCare Parent App](/docs/kindercare-parent-app).

